# Care Assistant - Project Context

Medical symptom tracking web app (French UI) with daily logging, reporting, and data visualization.

## Tech Stack

- **Framework**: Next.js 16 (App Router) + React 19 + TypeScript 5
- **Database**: SQLite via Prisma 7 ORM + LibSQL adapter (local file dev, Turso in production)
- **Auth**: NextAuth v5 (beta) with Google provider, JWT session strategy
- **UI**: Tailwind CSS v4 + shadcn/ui (New York style) + Radix UI + Lucide icons
- **Charts**: Recharts 3
- **Dates**: date-fns with French locale (`fr`)
- **Toasts**: Sonner

## Project Structure

```
src/app/           → Pages (App Router) and API route handlers
src/components/    → Feature components + ui/ (shadcn primitives)
src/lib/           → auth.ts, prisma.ts, types.ts, date-utils.ts, utils.ts
src/generated/     → Prisma client (auto-generated, never edit)
prisma/            → schema.prisma, migrations/
scripts/           → DB init and production migration helpers
```

## Key Conventions

- All UI text is in **French**
- Path alias: `@/*` maps to `./src/*`
- All data routes require authentication via `getAuthenticatedUserId()` from `@/lib/auth`
- Prisma client singleton in `@/lib/prisma` (dev: hot-reload safe via `globalThis`)
- Dates stored as ISO strings, displayed with `date-fns` French locale
- IDs use `cuid()` (Prisma default)
- Environment: `DATABASE_URL`, `DATABASE_AUTH_TOKEN`, `AUTH_SECRET`, `AUTH_GOOGLE_ID`, `AUTH_GOOGLE_SECRET`

## Documentation Maintenance (MANDATORY)

After every code change, check if documentation needs updating. Apply updates **in the same response** as the code change.

### What triggers an update

| Change type | Files to update |
|---|---|
| New/modified API route | `api-routes.mdc` (route table) + `README.md` (API table) |
| New/modified component | `react-components.mdc` (component table) + `README.md` (architecture tree) |
| Prisma schema change | `prisma-database.mdc` (model table) + `README.md` (data model + architecture) |
| New shared type | `typescript-types.mdc` |
| New env variable | This file (environment list) + `README.md` (env section) |
| New dependency or version bump | This file (tech stack) + `README.md` (stack table) |
| New page or route | `README.md` (architecture tree) |
| New script | `README.md` (scripts table) |
| UI pattern change | `ui-styling.mdc` |

### Rules

- Keep all doc files concise: update existing entries, don't duplicate
- If a feature is removed, remove it from docs too
- Never skip doc updates — they are part of the task, not a follow-up
